 "notes": [],
 "observations": [
  "The title page: sixteen centred lines in several typefaces and sizes, a rule under the series (159.1-427.7 pt, at 186.0 pt), a short rule under the part (267.8-318.6 pt, at 568.1 pt) and a dash between the address and the year (288.4-296.6 pt, at 713.3 pt). The typefaces are not imitated: each line is set in the edition's Latin font and scaled to the box of the printed line; bold is kept where the print is bold (L03, L06, L12, L14).",
  "L03: «Parte» in upper and lower case, the rest in capitals. L04: «sive» in small capitals; macrons over the second A and the last I of BATTĀNĪ (252.7-281.9 pt, at 211.3-212.8 pt). L09 and the publisher's name on L13 are letter-spaced. L13: «Prostat apud» in capitals and small capitals. L15: «in xysto christophoriano, nn.» in small capitals, the numbers 58-63 in full-height figures.",
  "Not part of the print and not transcribed: the perforated stamp of the library that held the scanned copy (UNIVERSITY LIBRARY PRINCETON, N. J., at the right, 568-645 pt), a few faint marks between L09 and L10 (near 505 pt) and the specks of the scan."
 ]
